---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GameGrid from '../components/GameGrid.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import CategoryLinks from '../components/CategoryLinks.astro';
import { games, categoryGames, canonical, gamePath, itemListSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/catalog.mjs';
const sledGames = categoryGames('sledding-games');
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What are the best free sled games to play online?',
    a: 'Choose from Sled Rider, Snow Rider 2, Gnome Bobsled, Sled Line, and Sleigh O’Balance. The first two offer downhill survival runs; Gnome Bobsled adds timed ice-track racing, Sled Line lets you draw the route, and Sleigh O’Balance challenges you to balance a load of gifts. Read each guide to pick the challenge you prefer.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to download anything to play sled games?',
    a: 'No app installation is needed. Open a card for its guide and play option. Most games have an embedded browser player with a Reload button if loading stalls. Sleigh O’Balance opens on the author’s official page. Keep JavaScript enabled when playing either way.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I play sled games on a phone?',
    a: 'Support varies by game. Snow Rider 2 is listed for iOS and Android browsers, Gnome Bobsled offers mobile touch controls, and Sled Line supports drawing with a finger. Sleigh O’Balance uses mouse controls, so choose a computer for that game. Check the controls on the game page before starting.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between a sled game and a snowboard game?',
    a: 'A sled game puts you on a sled or sleigh; a snowboard game puts a rider on a board. Similar snowy scenery does not mean identical rules: snowboard games here include both survival challenges and finish-line courses. Browse the Snowboard Games category to compare those options.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are these sled games free?',
    a: 'Yes. There is no Sled Games access fee or account requirement. The guides lead to free browser games, either embedded here or on the author’s official page for Sleigh O’Balance. Third-party platforms may show advertisements and set their own in-game terms.',
  },
];
---
<Layout snowfall title="Sled Games - Play Free Sledding Games Online" description="Play free sled games: Sled Rider, Snow Rider 2, Gnome Bobsled, Sled Line, and Sleigh O’Balance. Race on ice, draw routes, or balance a loaded sleigh." schema={[{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Sled Games', url: canonical('/') }, itemListSchema(sledGames, 'Sled Games'), faqSchema(faqs)]}>
  <section class="page-intro hub-intro">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">PICK YOUR NEXT CHALLENGE</span><h1>Sled Games</h1><p>Choose a downhill run, an ice-track race, a drawing challenge, or a sleigh-balancing game. Compare the controls and open one of the sled games below, or use the quick-start button to make a choice.</p></div>
    {sledGames.length > 0 && <a class="button" data-random-game href={gamePath(sledGames[0].slug)}>Play now <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>}
  </section>
  <section class="featured-games" aria-labelledby="sled-games-collection">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><h2 id="sled-games-collection">Choose your sled game</h2><p>Five ways to race, draw, slide, and balance, each with its own page and guide.</p></div></div>
    <GameGrid games={sledGames} eager />
  </section>
  <article class="content-section hub-guide prose" aria-label="Choosing sled games">
    <section aria-labelledby="what-are-sled-games">
      <h2 id="what-are-sled-games">What are sled games?</h2>
      <p>Sled games build a challenge around a sled or sleigh. That can mean steering down an open slope, racing through an ice channel, drawing a safe path, or keeping gifts balanced as the sleigh moves. The vehicle connects these games, while their goals and controls give you different ways to play.</p>
      <p>This collection includes <a href={gamePath('sled-rider')}>Sled Rider</a>, <a href={gamePath('snow-rider-2')}>Snow Rider 2</a>, <a href={gamePath('gnome-bobsled')}>Gnome Bobsled</a>, <a href={gamePath('sled-line')}>Sled Line</a>, and <a href={gamePath('sleigh-o-balance')}>Sleigh O’Balance</a>. The Snow Rider 2 guide explains that its player runs Snow Rider 3D, so you can check which release you are opening before starting.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="pick-a-sled-game">
      <h2 id="pick-a-sled-game">How to pick a sled game</h2>
      <h3>Endless runners vs level-based games</h3>
      <p>The first choice is the kind of goal you want. Sled Rider and Snow Rider 2 ask you to keep a downhill run alive while collecting gifts. Gnome Bobsled gives you ice tracks to finish against the clock: time your push at the start, take the bends, and compare a run with your own best-record ghost.</p>
      <p>For a different kind of challenge, Sled Line lets you draw roads that guide the sled past gaps and slopes. Sleigh O’Balance asks you to distribute gifts across a sleigh and respond to falling anvils. Browse <a href="/games/">All Winter Games</a> when you want to compare these with skiing, snowboarding, and other festive adventures.</p>
      <h3>Keyboard or touch controls</h3>
      <p>Check your device before choosing a game. Sled Rider and Snow Rider 2 use steering and jumping inputs. Gnome Bobsled adds a timed push at the start, cornering, and braking, with keyboard or mobile touch controls. Sled Line uses a mouse or finger to draw the road. Read each game’s controls table before you begin.</p>
      <p>Sleigh O’Balance uses mouse controls: place gifts and decide when an anvil can help counterbalance the load. Choose a computer for this game. A mobile compatibility listing for one game does not establish support for the whole collection, so use the visible prompts and the individual guide to choose a comfortable setup.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="sled-games-beginners">
      <h2 id="sled-games-beginners">Sled games for beginners</h2>
      <p>For a first session, choose one game and read its controls table before pressing play. <a href={gamePath('sled-rider')}>Sled Rider</a> is a useful starting point if you want a guide that breaks a run into starting, steering, jumping, collecting, and retrying. Its game page has the complete walkthrough.</p>
      <p>In a downhill runner, give your first few attempts one goal: stay on open snow. Saving every present can pull you into a turn you have not prepared for. Once steering feels predictable, add gift collecting to your next attempt. In Gnome Bobsled, practice the starting push and then learn one bend at a time before chasing a faster finish.</p>
      <p>Take a slower approach to Sled Line by planning a smooth route before drawing it. In Sleigh O’Balance, watch how each gift changes the load and weigh it against an anvil drop on the other side. Each game rewards a different habit, so use its own guide rather than carrying the same controls and strategy into every new challenge.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <section class="editorial-note">
    <h2>Find your next winter game</h2>
    <p>Pick a sled game from the collection above, or browse our <a href="/snowboard-games/">snowboard</a>, <a href="/ski-games/">ski</a>, and <a href="/christmas-games/">Christmas game</a> categories for something different.</p>
    <p>Visit the <a href="/games/">full winter collection</a> to see every game in one place: {games.map((game, index) => <Fragment>{index > 0 && (index === games.length - 1 ? ', and ' : ', ')}<a href={gamePath(game.slug)}>{game.title}</a></Fragment>)}.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/about/">About Sled Games →</a>
  </section>
  <Faq faqs={faqs} />
  <CategoryLinks />
  <script is:inline>
  {
    const randomStart = document.querySelector('[data-random-game]');
    randomStart?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const choices = document.querySelectorAll('.featured-games .game-card');
      const choice = choices[Math.floor(Math.random() * choices.length)];
      if (choice) randomStart.href = choice.href;
    });
  }
  </script>
</Layout>
